      "text": "# Safe Offline Archive Importer\n\n## Design Overview\n\nThis implementation provides a secure, robust ZIP archive importer that addresses common security vulnerabilities and reliability concerns when extracting archives from untrusted sources. The key design principles are:\n\n1. **Path Normalization & Traversal Prevention**: Reject any entry whose normalized path escapes the target directory.\n2. **Symlink/Hardlink Safety**: Never create symlinks or hardlinks during extraction; treat them as regular files or reject them.\n3. **Size Limits**: Enforce maximum uncompressed size, compressed size, and total archive size to prevent zip bombs.\n4. **Streaming Extraction**: Process entries one at a time without loading entire archives into memory.\n5. **Atomic Publication**: Extract to a temporary directory, then atomically rename to the final destination.\n6. **Interrupted Extraction Handling**: Use journaling/cleanup to handle crashes or interruptions gracefully.\n7. **No External Dependencies**: Pure Python, no reliance on system `unzip` or external tools.\n\n## Security Threats Addressed\n\n| Threat | Mitigation |\n|--------|-----------|\n| Path traversal (`../../etc/passwd`) | Normalize paths, reject absolute paths, reject `..` components |\n| Zip bomb (huge uncompressed size) | Enforce per-entry and total size limits |\n| Symlink attacks | Never create symlinks; reject entries with symlink attributes |\n| Hardlink attacks | Never create hardlinks |\n| Partial extraction on crash | Atomic rename after full extraction; cleanup temp dir on failure |\n| Resource exhaustion | Limit number of entries, total size, compression ratio |\n| Unicode normalization attacks | Normalize filenames, reject control characters |\n\n## Implementation\n\n```python\n\"\"\"\nSafe offline archive importer for ZIP files.\n\nThis module provides a secure, robust ZIP extraction utility that protects\nagainst common archive-based attacks including path traversal, zip bombs,\nsymlink attacks, and resource exhaustion.\n\nKey features:\n- Path normalization and traversal prevention\n- Symlink/hardlink rejection\n- Configurable size limits (per-entry, total, compression ratio)\n- Streaming extraction (no full archive in memory)\n- Atomic publication via temp directory + rename\n- Interrupted extraction cleanup\n- No external dependencies\n\"\"\"\n\nimport binascii\nimport io\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport stat\nimport struct\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport threading\nimport time\nimport warnings\nfrom pathlib import Path, PurePosixPath, PureWindowsPath\nfrom typing import Optional, Iterator, BinaryIO, Union, List, Tuple\n\ntry:\n    import zlib\n    crc32 = zlib.crc32\nexcept ImportError:\n    zlib = None\n    crc32 = binascii.crc32\n\ntry:\n    import bz2\nexcept ImportError:\n    bz2 = None\n\ntry:\n    import lzma\nexcept ImportError:\n    lzma = None\n\n\n# ============================================================================\n# Constants\n# ============================================================================\n\nZIP_STORED = 0\nZIP_DEFLATED = 8\nZIP_BZIP2 = 12\nZIP_LZMA = 14\n\n# Default safety limits\nDEFAULT_MAX_ENTRY_SIZE = 100 * 1024 * 1024       # 100 MB per entry\nDEFAULT_MAX_TOTAL_SIZE = 1 * 1024 * 1024 * 1024  # 1 GB total\nDEFAULT_MAX_COMPRESSION_RATIO = 100               # max uncompressed/compressed\nDEFAULT_MAX_ENTRIES = 10000                       # max number of entries\nDEFAULT_MAX_COMMENT_SIZE = 65536                  # 64 KB\n\n# ZIP format constants\nZIP64_LIMIT = (1 << 31) - 1\nZIP_FILECOUNT_LIMIT = (1 << 16) - 1\nZIP_MAX_COMMENT = (1 << 16) - 1\n\nstructEndArchive = b\"<4s4H2LH\"\nstringEndArchive = b\"PK\\005\\006\"\nsizeEndCentDir = struct.calcsize(structEndArchive)\n\nstructCentralDir = \"<4s4B4HL2L5H2L\"\nstringCentralDir = b\"PK\\001\\002\"\nsizeCentralDir = struct.calcsize(structCentralDir)\n\nstructFileHeader = \"<4s2B4HL2L2H\"\nstringFileHeader = b\"PK\\003\\004\"\nsizeFileHeader = struct.calcsize(structFileHeader)\n\nstructEndArchive64Locator = \"<4sLQL\"\nstringEndArchive64Locator = b\"PK\\x06\\x07\"\nsizeEndCentDir64Locator = struct.calcsize(structEndArchive64Locator)\n\nstructEndArchive64 = \"<4sQ2",
